CPython for Python code cells (docs/adr/0179)

Source:  https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.14.7/Python-3.14.7.tar.xz
Version: VERSION (3.14.7)
SHA256:  SHA256 (checked against the python.org release-file metadata)
License: LICENSE (PSF License Version 2 and the notices CPython ships)

The source tarball is not committed. `make` builds it with
scripts/cpython_runtime.sh into <BUILD>/cpython-<version>-<ABI>-<flags>/: a static
libpython with only the interpreter core and its bootstrap modules, no
docstrings, ensurepip, test modules, mimalloc, remote-debug attach or
libintl, plus frozen `encodings` modules. The executable needs no stdlib
directory and no system Python. `make fetch-cpython` downloads the pinned
tarball (a hash mismatch always fails); CPYTHON_TARBALL=/path supplies a
local copy, and CPYTHON_FETCH=0 forbids any download.

To update: change VERSION and SHA256 together from python.org metadata,
refresh LICENSE from the new tarball, rebuild, and rerun `make test`, the
Python conformance cases and the frozen-corpus replay.

### Unicode parser bootstrap
The builtin unicodedata module is statically linked and preloaded for the
CPython parser's non-ASCII identifier normalization and named Unicode escapes.
It is not a general import permission or an external stdlib dependency. A
production regression verifies Greek identifiers, NFKC normalization and named
Unicode escapes while user imports remain refused. Earlier minimal-probe sizes
remain historical; the final production artifact includes this required module.
